 hormonal and nutritional factors.", "SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL EN EL PACIENTE CON CIRUGÍA ONCOLÓGICA DE ESTÓMAGO, ESÓFAGO Y PÁNCREAS:A medical topic addressing nutritional support for patients undergoing oncological surgeries of the stomach, esophagus, and pancreas.", "VALORACIÓN Y SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL EN EL PACIENTE ONCOLÓGICO:A medical topic that emphasizes the assessment and nutritional support necessary for oncology patients.", "SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL EN EL PACIENTE HEMATOLÓGICO:A medical topic focusing on nutritional support for hematological patients, particularly those undergoing bone marrow transplants and dealing with graft-versus-host disease.", "DIFICULTADES NUTRICIONALES:A medical topic discussing the nutritional difficulties faced by patients with head and neck tumors, including issues like dysphagia.", "ALTERACIONES CICATRIZ:A medical topic discussing the complications related to healing and scarring in patients undergoing oncological surgeries.)<|COMPLETE|>", "NUTRICIÓN EN ONCOLOGÍA:NUTRICIÓN EN ONCOLOGÍA is a specialized field of study that addresses the nutritional needs and interventions for cancer patients. This discipline emphasizes the critical importance of screening and diagnosing malnutrition, which can significantly impact patient outcomes. It focuses on the dietary practices and recommendations necessary for cancer patients, particularly during and after treatments such as chemotherapy, hematopoietic cell transplants, and surgical procedures.\n\nThe field recognizes the unique nutritional challenges faced by patients, especially those undergoing treatment for head and neck tumors, and aims to enhance recovery and improve the quality of life through tailored dietary strategies. Nutritional support in oncology encompasses managing the dietary needs of patients before, during, and after treatment, including the implementation of nutritional guidelines and protocols for post-surgical care. This comprehensive approach ensures that cancer patients receive the necessary nutritional interventions to optimize their health and recovery throughout their treatment journey.", "ÍNDICE DE DETSKY:The Detsky index is a nutritional assessment tool used to evaluate the nutritional status of cancer patients.", "ALTERACIONES CICATRIZACIÓN:Alteraciones cicatrización are complications in wound healing that can arise from poor nutritional status in cancer patients.", "DESCENSO MASA MAGRA:Descenso masa magra refers to the loss of lean body mass, which is a common issue in patients with dysphagia and malnutrition.", "INCREMENTO DE INFECCIONES:Incremento de infecciones indicates the increased risk of infections due to malnutrition and immunodeficiency in cancer patients.", "DESCENSO DEL ESTATUS FUNCIONAL:Descenso del estatus funcional refers to the decline in a patient's ability to perform daily activities, often linked to malnutrition.", "DESCENSO DE LA HABILIDAD DE DEGLUTIR:Descenso de la habilidad de deglutir is a direct consequence of dysphagia, impacting the nutritional intake of patients.", "ENDOSCOPIA ALTA CON FIBRA ÓPTICA:High fiber optic endoscopy is a technique used to evaluate vocal cord function and swallowing dynamics", "ÍNDICE NUTRICIONAL DE PINATO:The Nutritional Index of Pinato (PNI) is a scoring system used to assess nutritional status based on serum albumin and lymphocyte count", "PACIENTES CON TUMORES DE CABEZA Y CUELLO:Patients suffering from head and neck tumors who may experience nutritional challenges and swallowing difficulties"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}